---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { dateStyle: 'long' }).format(new Date('2026-11-12'));
---

<TextPage
  title="Terms and Conditions | HearMyMic"
  description="The terms for using HearMyMic, a free online microphone and webcam test. Covers acceptable use, approximate results, and limits of liability."
  path="/terms"
  h1="Terms and conditions"
  crumb="Terms"
>
  <p class="text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <p>
    By using <span translate="no">HearMyMic</span> (hearmymic.com) you agree to these terms. If you don’t agree, please
    don’t use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does</h2>
  <p>
    <span translate="no">HearMyMic</span> is a free tool that tests your microphone and camera in your web browser. It
    also publishes guides to help you fix common microphone problems.
  </p>

  <h2>Results are approximate</h2>
  <p>
    Levels, ratings, device details and latency figures come from what your browser reports. They are a practical guide,
    not a calibrated measurement, and they can differ from what other apps or people hear. Don’t rely on them for
    professional, medical or safety-critical decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>Your audio and video</h2>
  <p>
    Audio and video are processed in your browser and are not uploaded to our servers. See the
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Interfere with or disrupt the site, or try to gain unauthorized access to it.</li>
    <li>Copy the site in bulk, or use automated tools to overload it.</li>
    <li>Use the site for anything unlawful.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design and code of this site belong to its owner. You may link to any page and quote short extracts with a
    link back. Please don’t republish whole pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Guides and advice</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides describe settings in third-party products such as Windows, macOS, browsers, Zoom, Discord, Teams and Xbox.
    Menus change between versions, so the steps may not match exactly what you see. Follow them at your own risk, and
    check the maker’s own documentation if something looks different.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to other websites and may use third-party services such as analytics. We don’t control them and
    aren’t responsible for their content or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind. We don’t promise that it will be
    uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for your particular device or purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Limit of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent the law allows, we’re not liable for any loss or damage that results from using, or being
    unable to use, the site, including problems that follow from changing settings on your devices.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows when they last changed, and continued use of
    the site means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
